---
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { rippleShader } from "../demos/ripple-shader";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteUrl, url } from "../site";

const llmsFull = new URL(url("llms-full.txt"), siteUrl).href;

const llmsPrompt = `
Read ${llmsFull} first.
Then add a glitch effect to the hero image with @vfx-js/core.
`;

const prompts = [
    {
        label: "Image hover",
        text: `Use @vfx-js/react to add an rgbShift effect to the product images in ProductCard.
Make the shift stronger while the mouse is over the image. Use a uniform function that reads a ref.`,
    },
    {
        label: "Text intro",
        text: `Make the h1 on the landing page glitch in when it scrolls into view, then settle.
Use @vfx-js/core with a custom shader driven by enterProgress. Give it 50 px of overflow.`,
    },
    {
        label: "Effect chain",
        text: `Add PixelateEffect, then BloomEffect from @vfx-js/effects to the background video.
Make one VFX for the page and new Effect instances per element.`,
    },
    {
        label: "Vue / Nuxt",
        text: `In this Nuxt app, put a halftone effect on every image in the blog post body with the v-vfx directive from @vfx-js/vue.
Images come from our CDN; make sure CORS works.`,
    },
];

const writePrompt = `
Write a VFX-JS custom shader for vfx.add.
The image ripples like water around the mouse.
Use the built-in mouse and time uniforms. GLSL ES 3.0.
`;

const addCode = `
// rippleShader holds the GLSL above as a string.
await vfx.add(img, { shader: rippleShader, wrap: "clamp" });
`;

const checks = [
    {
        title: "Console errors",
        body: "A shader that fails to compile makes vfx.add reject with the GL error log and the full source. Catch it with .catch(console.error) and paste the log back to the agent.",
    },
    {
        title: "A blank element",
        body: "Usually the shader failed, the image is blocked by CORS, or the element has zero size.",
    },
    {
        title: "Cut-off effect",
        body: "A shader draws only inside the element unless you set overflow. Effects set their own room with outputRect, or a pad param on built-in ones.",
        link: { href: "how-it-works/#overflow", label: "Overflow" },
    },
    {
        title: "Stale text",
        body: "Text and other elements are captured once. The agent must call vfx.update(el) after the content changes.",
        link: { href: "how-it-works/#capture", label: "Element capture" },
    },
    {
        title: "Many VFX instances",
        body: "Each VFX has its own WebGL context. Ask for one per page, made in client code.",
        link: { href: "how-it-works/#limits", label: "Limits" },
    },
    {
        title: "Screenshots",
        body: "Agents can't see the canvas. Ask for a Playwright script that takes a screenshot. Headless browsers need WebGL on.",
    },
];
---

<Layout
    page="ai"
    description="Let your AI agent add VFX-JS effects and write shaders, with the VFX-JS skill or llms.txt."
>
    <h1>Use with AI</h1>
    <p>
        Coding agents can add VFX-JS effects and write shaders for you. Give them
        the docs first, so they use the current API.
    </p>

    <section id="skill">
        <h2>Install the skill</h2>
        <p>
            The VFX-JS skill works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and other agents
            that read skills. Run this in your project:
        </p>
        <CodeBlock code="npx skills add fand/vfx-js" lang="bash" label="Terminal" />
        <p>
            The agent reads it when a task needs it. It covers every package (core,
            React, Vue, Svelte, Astro, effects, transitions), the shader presets,
            custom shaders, the Effect API, transitions, and common pitfalls.
            The source is
            <a href="https://github.com/fand/vfx-js/tree/main/skills/vfx-js" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">skills/vfx-js</a>
            on GitHub.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="llms">
        <h2>llms.txt</h2>
        <p>No skill support? Give the agent one of these files.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href={url("llms.txt")}>llms.txt</a>: a short overview, a quick
                start, and links to each part of the docs.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href={url("llms-full.txt")}>llms-full.txt</a>: the whole skill in
                one file. Paste it into a chat, or point the agent to the URL.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <CodeBlock code={llmsPrompt} lang="plaintext" label="Prompt" />
    </section>

    <section id="prompts">
        <h2>Prompts that work</h2>
        <p>
            Name the package, the element, and the effect. Say what should happen
            on scroll or hover.
        </p>
        <div class="Prompts">
            {
                prompts.map((prompt) => (
                    <CodeBlock
                        code={prompt.text}
                        lang="plaintext"
                        label={prompt.label}
                    />
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="write">
        <h2>Write a shader with AI</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Describe the look in words. Ask for a VFX-JS custom shader.</li>
            <li>
                Paste the GLSL into <code>vfx.add(el, &#123; shader &#125;)</code>.
            </li>
            <li>Look at it in the browser. Tell the agent what to change.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="Prompts">
            <CodeBlock code={writePrompt} lang="plaintext" label="Prompt" />
        </div>
        <p>The agent returns something like this:</p>
        <CodeBlock code={rippleShader} lang="glsl" label="GLSL" />
        <CodeBlock code={addCode} lang="ts" label="main.ts" />
        <p>Move the mouse over the image:</p>
        <div class="Demo">
            <img
                id="RippleDemo"
                src={url("images/jellyfish.webp")}
                alt="A jellyfish that ripples around the mouse"
            />
        </div>
        <p>
            The agent can use <code>time</code>, <code>mouse</code>,
            <code>resolution</code>, <code>offset</code>,
            <code>intersection</code>, <code>enterProgress</code> and more. See
            <a href={url("how-it-works/#uniforms")}>Uniforms and timing</a> for the
            full list, and <a href={url("shaders/")}>Custom Shaders</a> for
            multipass and post effects.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="check">
        <h2>Check the result</h2>
        <p>The agent writes the code but can't watch it run. Look for these.</p>
        <dl class="Checks">
            {
                checks.map((check) => (
                    <div>
                        <dt>{check.title}</dt>
                        <dd>
                            {check.body}
                            {check.link && (
                                <>
                                    {" "}
                                    See <a href={url(check.link.href)}>{check.link.label}</a>.
                                </>
                            )}
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                ))
            }
        </dl>
    </section>
</Layout>

<script>
    import { lazyDemo } from "../demos/lazy";
    import { rippleShader } from "../demos/ripple-shader";
    import { onPage } from "../lifecycle";

    onPage(() => {
        const ripple = document.getElementById("RippleDemo");
        if (ripple) {
            lazyDemo(ripple, () => ({ shader: rippleShader, wrap: "clamp" }));
        }
    });
</script>

<style>
    /* Prompts are prose. Wrap them instead of scrolling. */
    .Prompts :global(pre) {
        white-space: pre-wrap;
    }
    .Demo {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        padding: 48px 32px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .Demo img {
        width: min(100%, 480px);
    }
    .Checks {
        margin: 24px 0;
    }
    .Checks div {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 16px;
        padding: 12px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .Checks dt {
        font-weight: 600;
    }
    .Checks dt,
    .Checks dd {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.125rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    @media (max-width: 767px) {
        .Checks div {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            gap: 4px;
        }
    }
</style>
